  "_note": "The recipe table -- V4.6's content. One entry per production route: `inputs` maps a good id to the quantity consumed per unit of `output`, and `labour_per_unit` / `capital_per_unit` are the two factor requirements per unit, positive and in the same arbitrary scale as goods.json's base_price. RAW AND AGRI CARRY NO RECIPE -- they are primary producers whose `inputs` is empty by the model rather than by an omission, and so do the ten services (and `tourism`, which is a service wearing a consumer label). Several goods carry MORE THAN ONE route on purpose: gas, coal and nuclear power are three genuine ways to make a kilowatt-hour, and basic-oxygen versus electric-arc are two genuine ways to make a tonne of steel -- a nation's mix is a mix of routes, not a second grade of the same one. Every input and every output must be a good in goods.json; src/core/data_loader.gd refuses the file otherwise, because an input nobody declares would sit here looking like a recipe and produce nothing at tick time. See docs/commodities-model.md.",
